        {
          "file": "tests/frontier-comparison-analysis.test.mjs",
          "tests": 20,
          "passed": 20,
          "topLevel": [
            "the analysis reads the roles, the slots and the sentences of the protocol, and refuses a protocol it does not understand",
            "the median is the protocol's (the mean of the two middle values), not the nearest rank of the oracle, and the idle reference is the median of the half-sums",
            "the module reproduces the protocol's fixed interval and its known answer, with the parameters read from the protocol",
            "the four categories, the non-inferior flag beside them, and H1 and H2 as estimates with no category",
            "the margin is the larger of 10% of B's median and the floor of 0.5 ms: the same difference is a cost under the floor and neutral under 10%",
            "a hand-checkable campaign: arms with no spread give point intervals and the differences of the medians",
            "the report recomputes from its own per-run values: the intervals and the p-values are the bootstrap of the right arms in the right order",
            "the Holm guard downgrades a category whose claim does not stand in the family of four windows, and shows the unadjusted one beside it",
            "the axes: the verdict of C against B with the outcome's own margin, the deterministic package size and the single observation of the cost of change",
            "FPS without a limit: higher is better, a gain excludes zero, and the axis is N/A when the vsync does not read DISABLED",
            "the descriptive outcomes report medians, interquartile ranges and intervals with no category, and leave the warm-up out",
            "the absolute budgets: met when at most the frozen value, exceeded otherwise, and N/A for the stress window the freeze left N/A",
            "when arm B is not ready the report is A against C: H1 only, no category for H3 and no gain claimed",
            "the parameters are read from the protocol when the script runs: a changed protocol changes the interval, the margin and the load limit",
            "the report has the sections of the protocol in order, the frozen values and the hash of the protocol, and takes its words from the campaign",
            "the same campaign gives the same report byte for byte, and the seed of the protocol is in it",
            "the command line writes the report of a campaign file, checks its format and refuses a bad one",
            "the example report of the evidence record is the exact output of the script for the synthetic campaign regenerated with the same seed, by the commands of its README",
            "the unreported example of the evidence record is the exact output of its command, and is the validity section of the report of a campaign with an attempt that wrote no report",
            "the protocol's test imports the functions from the modules, and the tests are part of the contracts"
          ]
        },
        {
          "file": "tests/frontier-comparison-validity.test.mjs",
          "tests": 11,
          "passed": 11,
          "topLevel": [
            "a load above the limit is rejected with its reading and redone in the same slot, and the rejected attempt does not count",
            "an execution that did not draw or was not paced in the presented lane is rejected with the reason, and the same data in the unlimited lane is not",
            "an incomplete window or idle window, a wrong hash, a wrong seed or a Debug build, an error and a parity mismatch are each rejected with their rule",
            "the fourth attempt, or three rejected ones, stop the campaign and no statistic is produced",
            "a repeat of the other game in one arm stops the campaign, in either lane, and an instrument that did not pass counts nothing",
            "the order of the executions: slots follow the protocol's sequence, the planned and accepted counts balance by position, and an arm with too few executions is incomplete",
            "attempts that contradict one another, or data that are not in the format, are refused and not analysed",
            "an attempt that wrote no report is in the format: a valid entry is accepted and each wrong field is refused",
            "an attempt that wrote no report is rejected by the errors rule with its clause and values, counts as an attempt of its slot, and has its load readings and no vsync",
            "the attempts of a slot are numbered 1, 2, ... without gaps over the executions and the unreported together; a gap, a repeat or an attempt after the accepted one is a problem",
            "three attempts that wrote no report use up the slot and stop the campaign by the attempts rule of the analysis, and a fourth is over the limit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "file": "tests/frontier-comparison-campaign.test.mjs",
          "tests": 20,
          "passed": 20,
          "topLevel": [
            "a campaign plays the protocol's sequence in both lanes, once per slot, one process at a time, balanced by position, and its campaign is in the format the analysis reads",
            "a load above the limit, an undrawn presented window and an incomplete window are each rejected with their reason, kept in the raw data and redone in the same slot",
            "an error and a process that wrote no report are rejected by the errors rule and redone; the one without a report is in the campaign's unreported, counts in its slot and in the report",
            "a process that timed out and one that exited 0 without a report are unreported too, each with how it ended",
            "three attempts that wrote no report in a slot stop the campaign by the attempts rule of the analysis, as three rejected executions do",
            "three rejected attempts in a slot stop the campaign: the later slots do not run, the stop is recorded and the analysis produces no statistic",
            "the other game once is redone; the second time in the same arm stops the campaign",
            "a scenario that waited with numbers other than the protocol's stops the campaign, chosen by the problem's code, and the analysis alone would not have seen it",
            "a protocol whose load limit is not a finite positive number is refused before anything runs, because the wait could never tell a quiet machine",
            "the wait for the load reads it every few seconds until it is under the limit, records the wait, and a wait that runs out lets the attempt run to be judged by the rule",
            "a campaign interrupted after the k-th attempt, or twice, resumes from the first open slot and ends as a campaign that was never interrupted",
            "a campaign is not resumed if the protocol, the script, the binary, the package or the instrument has another hash, or the options are not the same; nothing runs and the state stays as it was",
            "the self-check is the gate: if it fails nothing runs, the stop is recorded, and a resume repeats it until it passes",
            "an engine or a renderer other than the one the self-check ran on stops the campaign",
            "the self-check runs in the lane the launcher runs in: a window for a launcher that opens one, headless for one that does not, and a check in the other lane is not the campaign's renderer",
            "the unlimited lane whose vsync does not read back DISABLED is N/A and is not run further, and says so",
            "a rehearsal redoes nothing, is marked as one and says in its deviations that it is not a result",
            "the Release launcher refuses with the reason, before anything is run or written",
            "the command line: --build debug and --slots are for a rehearsal, the numbers are checked, and a campaign needs its build and its directory",
            "a file is written whole or not at all"
          ]
        },
        {
          "file": "tests/frontier-comparison-campaign-state.test.mjs",
          "tests": 7,
